      <p class="paraCommon paraHeader"  >    <b>What education and skills help you get a green job? </b>
      <span style="font-size:18px;display:block;margin-top:10px;">Your learning path is way simpler than you think.</span>    
      </p>
      <p class="paraCommon">Most people assume green jobs need fancy degrees, elite colleges, or some “environment certification” that nobody can even explain properly. </p>
<p class="paraCommon">Truth bomb: <b>they don’t.</b></p>
 <p class="paraCommon"> In today’s world, any background — Science, Commerce, Arts, ITI, or even "I'm-currently-figuring-life-out" is perfectly okay.
</p> <p class="paraCommon"> Private green businesses don’t ask, <i>"Kahan se padha?"</i>
</p> <p class="paraCommon">
       They ask,<span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600">"Can you learn? Are you curious? Are you willing to grow?"</span> 
    </p>

    <p class="paraCommon"> And here’s the real shocker: <span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600">You can become green-job ready in just 70–100 hours of self-study.</span> Yup, not months, not years — hours. </p>
    <p class="paraCommon">The world’s best lessons, videos, tools, and tutorials are freely available online. No tuition fees. No coaching classes. No gatekeepers.</p>
    <p class="paraCommon">The Government is not hiring for green jobs.<span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600"> The private sector is; quietly, rapidly, and without obsession over degrees.</span></p>
    <p class="paraCommon">What they care about is <span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600">skills + attitude + your inclination to do meaningful work. </span> </p>
    <p class="paraCommon"></p>
    
   
